{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened","id":574570,"title":"Second Edition Wizened","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T18:36:14-07:00","id":574570,"title":"Second Edition Wizened","content":"Here's the thread to chat over them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-wizened/\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the rough draft</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 06-30-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:06:13-07:00","id":574607,"title":"","content":"Frailty's a little harsh, especially if it's coupled with the supernatural complication.<br /> <br /> How about &quot;Fails her special talent in a way that has long-lasting consequences&quot;? (If it's mild difficulty it just becomes more interesting a task-an actual challenge to overcome, a risk that makes it exciting and glorious to triumph over).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:18:47-07:00","id":574613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574607#post574607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frailty's a little harsh, especially if it's coupled with the supernatural complication.<br /> <br /> How about &quot;Fails her special talent in a way that has long-lasting consequences&quot;? (If it's mild difficulty it just becomes more interesting a task-an actual challenge to overcome, a risk that makes it exciting and glorious to triumph over).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Their talent is probably going to be around a base 6-9 dice, without any equipment or anything involved. Failure's going to be rare. And Clarity breaking points aren't guaranteed losses; more often than not, they're not losses. All they really end up doing is giving you a Condition that builds a little drama, and gives you Beats. If anything, I feel like it won't come up enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:23:52-07:00","id":574614,"title":"","content":"Off of this, Wizened are coming off a lot more like Elementals from First edition, with physically incorporating things into them. I'm also finding it a bit hard to see how they've escaped... it feels like they're damaged in their time in Arcadia, so they make do by sowing themselves back up with whatever things that are around, but that doesn't seem to lead into the choice to escape that the new Seemings are attempting to do, as it feels like what they've been doing in Arcadia already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:35:02-07:00","id":574648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574614#post574614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off of this, Wizened are coming off a lot more like Elementals from First edition, with physically incorporating things into them. I'm also finding it a bit hard to see how they've escaped... it feels like they're damaged in their time in Arcadia, so they make do by sowing themselves back up with whatever things that are around, but that doesn't seem to lead into the choice to escape that the new Seemings are attempting to do, as it feels like what they've been doing in Arcadia already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be they used their talents to escape. Arcadia noticed they remade themselves in their skills' image, and gave them an opportunity to use it (a Wizened of Song awed a Gentry into letting them out, a Wizened of War devised a deliberate failure, a Wizened of Clockwork found a box of scraps, in a cave..).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:13:42-07:00","id":574666,"title":"","content":"Robocop is SO a Wizened holy shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:14:04-07:00","id":574667,"title":"","content":"So if Ogres are hurt people hurting people, it seems like the Wizened are kind of... autistic? Reminds me of a friend who'll skip lunch to work on projects, and gets uncomfortable around crowds and obsesses over perfection and how she doesn't have it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574614#post574614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off of this, Wizened are coming off a lot more like Elementals from First edition</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'll agree that it does seem a bit closer to the Manikin than anything like Chatelain or Soldier, it doesn't really feel very Elemental to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:14:18-07:00","id":574668,"title":"","content":"I sort of have trouble seeing them as wizened - in the sense of shrunken, reduced, or shriveled. The concept is pretty neat and is worthy of inclusion, but the name doesn't really suit the manifestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:35:34-07:00","id":574674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574668#post574668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sort of have trouble seeing them as wizened - in the sense of shrunken, reduced, or shriveled. The concept is pretty neat and is worthy of inclusion, but the name doesn't really suit the manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reduced in the pursuit of the thing you're good at? The artist who forgets to eat while working on his masterpiece? Who neglects himself in pursuit of his Thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:38:12-07:00","id":574676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574667#post574667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if Ogres are hurt people hurting people, it seems like the Wizened are kind of... autistic? Reminds me of a friend who'll skip lunch to work on projects, and gets uncomfortable around crowds and obsesses over perfection and how she doesn't have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even autistic, and I experience all these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:41:22-07:00","id":574678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574674#post574674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Reduced in the pursuit of the thing you're good at? The artist who forgets to eat while working on his masterpiece? Who neglects himself in pursuit of his Thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>i ami great example actually,i'm from south america and english is my second language. when i was 11 i decide i wanted to learn english,and i did. dedicated myself a LOT to it. after some time i knew more english than anybody else that i knew,now ask me how many friends i made on that time period","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:44:48-07:00","id":574681,"title":"","content":"There's a trend I've noticed in a couple of the Seeming Blessings and Curses that could be illusory (it's noticeably absent in the Fairest draft, for instance) but still seems significant:<br /> <br /> Your Blessing restores your Clarity in a way that reinforces the way you changed to escape Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Your Curse imperils your Clarity in a fashion that evokes the part of your background that got you there in the first place.<br /> <br /> The Beast speaks out of turn and remembers that liberating flight from Faerie that brought her back to Earth, but finds the surety of her footing wavers under the long shadow of her Keeper's nets.<br /> <br /> The Darkling stays sane playing guardian angel to his family in the wake his fetch's destruction, until the freehold oneiromancer sells them a week of restful sleep; he of all people should know better than to be taken in by a pristine reputation.<br /> <br /> The Ogre regains her composure when the the stalker's totaled car gets her point across, but remind her that her overattachment to her pets was what got her leg run over all those years ago and the limp comes back as strong as it was during her time as a Faerie carriagehorse.<br /> <br /> The Elemental knows that even his most erratic explorations of human stimulus serve a greater purpose \u2014 the addict whose relapse he induced was spared the poison that now wracks the dreams of their former coworkers \u2014 but he's forced to confront the possibility that he's lost the plot when his friend starts demonstrating withdrawal symptoms and growing apart from their family, and the chance that you've learned nothing is a disquieting prospect to the already half-immortal.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's deliberate, but I'd be interested to see if this observation bears out in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:46:04-07:00","id":574684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574681#post574681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a trend I've noticed in a couple of the Seeming Blessings and Curses that could be illusory (it's noticeably absent in the Fairest draft, for instance) but still seems significant:<br /> <br /> Your Blessing restores your Clarity in a way that reinforces the way you changed to escape Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Your Curse imperils your Clarity in a fashion that evokes the part of your background that got you there in the first place.<br /> <br /> The Beast speaks out of turn and remembers that liberating flight from Faerie that brought her back to Earth, but finds the surety of her footing wavers under the long shadow of her Keeper's nets.<br /> <br /> The Darkling stays sane playing guardian angel to his family in the wake his fetch's destruction, until the freehold oneiromancer sells them a week of restful sleep; he of all people should know better than to be taken in by a pristine reputation.<br /> <br /> The Ogre regains her composure when the the stalker's totaled car gets her point across, but remind her that her overattachment to her pets was what got her leg run over all those years ago and the limp comes back as strong as it was during her time as a Faerie carriagehorse.<br /> <br /> The Elemental knows that even his most erratic explorations of human stimulus serve a greater purpose \u2014 the addict whose relapse he induced was spared the poison that now wracks the dreams of their former coworkers \u2014 but he's forced to confront the possibility that he's lost the plot when his friend starts demonstrating withdrawal symptoms and growing apart from their family, and the chance that you've learned nothing is a disquieting prospect to the already half-immortal.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's deliberate, but I'd be interested to see if this observation bears out in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was absolutely deliberate. Good catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 06-30-2015, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:46:36-07:00","id":574685,"title":"","content":"This is really interesting. In many ways they are the opposite of 1e Wizened. In 1e, Wizened were taken to do something, and they were changed by their Keeper to be better suited to that task. Now, they did something before their Durance, and their Keeper took them away from that, and they escaped by remaking themselves in a way that would allow them to do that thing again. I actually really like this new take on it. It's very different, but definitely very cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:49:25-07:00","id":574687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574666#post574666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robocop is SO a Wizened holy shit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If so, which the most appropriate of the new Kiths?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:58:38-07:00","id":574689,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I don't know that I'm completely feeling this one yet. May need to roll it around a little more.<br /> <br /> All of the Seemings have a strong component of the Changeling leaving behind some personal trait that had held her back from escape. A Darkling gives up her trust, an Elemental gives up her ego, an Ogre gives up her willingness to feel, a Fairest gives up her passivity, a Beast gives up her civility, and a Wizened gives up... everything about her that's getting in the way of her craft?<br /> <br /> It's interesting, but I don't know that I find it as compelling or engaging as the other 5 in terms of characters produced. Then again, I'm also quite tired. Maybe it'll click better for me after a good night's sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:01:59-07:00","id":574691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574614#post574614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off of this, Wizened are coming off a lot more like Elementals from First edition, with physically incorporating things into them. I'm also finding it a bit hard to see how they've escaped... it feels like they're damaged in their time in Arcadia, so they make do by sowing themselves back up with whatever things that are around, but that doesn't seem to lead into the choice to escape that the new Seemings are attempting to do, as it feels like what they've been doing in Arcadia already.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that they're forcing order and rhythm and perfection upon Arcadia, and in doing so, are no longer a part of it. Their perception of Arcadia is Fickle Fate, that it's a tangled mess of chaos, but the core of the Wizened, the &quot;something inside the would-be Wizened&quot; is about correctness and sense.<br /> <br /> I think that's how I've settled on thinking about Seemings; they're not so much things you aspire to or really identify with (though they are that as well): they're what you've rejected. It's placing the blame of your Durance, of your pre-Durance life, upon something comprehensible and pushing it away. And in doing so, you're out. Is that entirely healthy? Not really, which would explain why the Escape is the <i>beginning</i> of the story, and not its end... but I think it's a good way to think about them, and it helps make sense of what a specific character's Escape demands from a psychological standpoint.<br /> <br /> It also means that you could work nearly any Seeming into the physical details of an Escape; as long as you set up the right psychological cues to riff off, you can get all six Seemings from the same set of actual events. That's something I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:03:12-07:00","id":574692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574689#post574689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a Wizened gives up... everything about her that's getting in the way of her craft?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inefficiency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:05:34-07:00","id":574693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574687#post574687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If so, which the most appropriate of the new Kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the new ones seems to fit. i think he's a manikin since a wizened manikin is discrebed as Although no trace of flesh remains, it's clear that this construct of brushed aluminum, colored wires, and advanced circuits was made by replacing portions of a human body one piece at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:26:01-07:00","id":574702,"title":"","content":"To be quite honest, I think this is probably my favourite of the new Seemings so far. The mechanics are simple and straight-forward, telling you all you need to know at a glance. The only issue I have is that the whole &quot;exceptional success on three instead of five for their unique craft&quot; treads dangerously close to rendering the Artist Kith semi-irrelevant for the Wizened. A Wizened Artist should seem <i>superlative</i>, not redundant. Might be best to include some benefit for Artists (are they considered to always get an Exceptional Success when pursuing their particular craft for self-comfort reasons?) to raise them above that level slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:32:04-07:00","id":574716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574702#post574702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be quite honest, I think this is probably my favourite of the new Seemings so far. The mechanics are simple and straight-forward, telling you all you need to know at a glance. The only issue I have is that the whole &quot;exceptional success on three instead of five for their unique craft&quot; treads dangerously close to rendering the Artist Kith semi-irrelevant for the Wizened. A Wizened Artist should seem <i>superlative</i>, not redundant. Might be best to include some benefit for Artists (are they considered to always get an Exceptional Success when pursuing their particular craft for self-comfort reasons?) to raise them above that level slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have two &quot;three instead of fives&quot;, I'll clarify that success = exceptional all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:32:42-07:00","id":574717,"title":"","content":"Wait, they gain a mechanical advantage on top of free Clarity - does that reflect a shift for the other Seemings too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:35:25-07:00","id":574720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574717#post574717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, they gain a mechanical advantage on top of free Clarity - does that reflect a shift for the other Seemings too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I haven't made it clear; the Seemings have all been sort of... format spitballing? I'm considering a few different routes here. I'm leaning toward: <br /> <br /> Benefits: <br /> <br /> 1) Coping mechanism/Clarity gain thing. <br /> <br /> 2) A mechanical boost to your escape thing. <br /> <br /> Drawbacks: <br /> <br /> 1) A thing that risks Clarity, adds to your list of risks. <br /> <br /> 2) A thing that makes your Changeling experience a little more complicated mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:37:38-07:00","id":574725,"title":"","content":"A Wizened Smith or Maker would appear to be quite impressive.<br /> <br /> Now that we have seen all the new Kiths and Seemings (except the 7th from Dark Eras), we should probably start a thread with the most optimized, thematically appropriate, or just plain entertaining combinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:38:16-07:00","id":574728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574676#post574676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even autistic, and I experience all these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but that is still something that an autistic person can relate to. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574684#post574684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was absolutely deliberate. Good catch.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the more problem with the Fairest one. I'm interested to see how you change that one, if for no other reason than they were my favourite kith. Being the &quot;normal&quot; looking ones and Dual Kithing allowed more freedom.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574687#post574687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, which the most appropriate of the new Kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Metalflesh, duh.<br /> \u2022 Wizened: Welded and riveted plates of bronze fit around what was once a human body, but which may no longer exist beneath the metal. <br /> Blessing: They gain armor equal to their Stamina and their fists and feet do lethal damage. If they spend a point of Glamour, for the next Scene they also convert Wyrd points of lethal damage they taking in a turn into bashing damage and gain armor piercing 1 on all strikes made with their hands and feet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:39:56-07:00","id":574729,"title":"","content":"Maybe the quote should be about the Tin Woodman?<br /> <br /> Alternately, something from Iron Man?<br /> <br /> Speaking of, which, now that we have all of them, which Seeming is which for the Avengers? And which is which for the Oz characters?<br /> <br /> I think that some examples of possible Durances for each Seeming would be nice, because I'm having a tough time visualizing how this would work or how rebuilding themselves with their tools helps them escape. Despite, yes, getting that both Iron Man and Nick Chopper are Wizened.<br /> <br /> The clarity break makes sense to me, though I worry that it might encourage more people to play Craft/Expression 5 Makers/Artists, instead of Craft/Expression 2 students, given how often said character is probably going to want to practice their art. I'm also curious if you have any thoughts on what their mechanical penalty might be? <br /> <br /> Possibly this is just my own bias, but this seems a bit focused on creators and makers, people who make physical things or who create art, but it seems like you could also do, say, a Wizened Truefriend who's thing was empathy and helping you out ...to the point that they completely ignore their own needs because they're too focused on the stuff they're doing for their Motley. And I'm not entirely sure that comes across in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:40:25-07:00","id":574730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574720#post574720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry if I haven't made it clear; the Seemings have all been sort of... format spitballing? I'm considering a few different routes here. I'm leaning toward:<br /> <br /> Benefits:<br /> <br /> 1) Coping mechanism/Clarity gain thing.<br /> <br /> 2) A mechanical boost to your escape thing.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) A thing that risks Clarity, adds to your list of risks.<br /> <br /> 2) A thing that makes your Changeling experience a little more complicated mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this route as it adds greater mechanical differentiation among characters and offers more role-playing opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:44:59-07:00","id":574731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574729#post574729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clarity break makes sense to me, though I worry that it might encourage more people to play Craft/Expression 5 Makers/Artists, instead of Craft/Expression 2 students, given how often said character is probably going to want to practice their art. I'm also curious if you have any thoughts on what their mechanical penalty might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If people want to crank their Skills to avoid their drawback, that's fine. Their &quot;drawback&quot; really means &quot;more Beats&quot;. So all they're doing is missing out. <br /> <br /> I think maybe once they start an extended action, they can't stop it without spending Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:45:07-07:00","id":574732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574729#post574729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly this is just my own bias, but this seems a bit focused on creators and makers, people who make physical things or who create art, but it seems like you could also do, say, a Wizened Truefriend who's thing was empathy and helping you out ...to the point that they completely ignore their own needs because they're too focused on the stuff they're doing for their Motley. And I'm not entirely sure that comes across in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, if their thing was being a good friend before they were taken, and they were taken to be a good friend, they would not feel the emptiness of not being able to do their thing during their durance that causes one to become a Wizened. They would probably just stay in Arcadia, happy to finally find a place where they are completely fulfilled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T21:52:47-07:00","id":574746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574687#post574687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If so, which the most appropriate of the new Kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Razorhand or Metalflesh, I think. But I don't know that much about Robocop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:15:23-07:00","id":574780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574732#post574732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if their thing was being a good friend before they were taken, and they were taken to be a good friend, they would not feel the emptiness of not being able to do their thing during their durance that causes one to become a Wizened. They would probably just stay in Arcadia, happy to finally find a place where they are completely fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Keeper can't truly appreciate their love. They can't make it happy, and it can't make them happy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574746#post574746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Razorhand or Metalflesh, I think. But I don't know that much about Robocop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it's right there in the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:19:16-07:00","id":574781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574732#post574732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if their thing was being a good friend before they were taken, and they were taken to be a good friend, they would not feel the emptiness of not being able to do their thing during their durance that causes one to become a Wizened. They would probably just stay in Arcadia, happy to finally find a place where they are completely fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the writeup itself speaks against that being an obstacle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Escape</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Durance isn\u2019t easy for anyone, but for the would-be Wizened the change is just too much. In the hands of her Keeper, there is no pattern, no safe routine to fall back to. No time to practice her craft or rhyme and reason to escape too. <b>Even if the Keeper brought the would-be Wizened to perform her art, the very nature of the unreality means that pattern, order, routine are impossible.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to be passionate about an art, to find oneself supernaturally augmented to carry it out, and still find it hollow and unsatisfying in Arcadia's climate. I mean, an atmosphere to freely practice an art is one thing. An atmosphere to practice an art while one of the Gentry waits to be impressed is quite another. &quot;As long as I'm here, I can't express myself, not really. Because if I don't express myself exactly the way my Keeper wants today... Ohh, no, no, no. I can't let myself think of what he'll do to me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor breakup. 07-01-2015, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:20:34-07:00","id":574783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574732#post574732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if their thing was being a good friend before they were taken, and they were taken to be a good friend, they would not feel the emptiness of not being able to do their thing during their durance that causes one to become a Wizened. They would probably just stay in Arcadia, happy to finally find a place where they are completely fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you put it that way, I agree with you. That character would only show up on Earth as a Loyalist.<br /> <br /> But, I think you're missing part of the point of the Seeming. It sounds like part of the point of the Wizened is that their Durance in Arcadia was both emotionally and physically damaging to them. Even if they were taken to do the stuff they love doing, either the nature of the place or their perception of it prevents them from being truly fulfilled there.<br /> <br /> Also, just because they were taken to use their special skill doesn't mean that the Keeper wants to use it in a way that the proto-Wizened will enjoy. For example, coming back to our Truefriend, maybe the person was taken because she was good with animals and just really, really liked them. As such, she's taken by a sadistic Keeper, who likes to watch her try to stop him from torturing other creatures. Each time she successfully interposes herself between the Keeper and his prey, the Keeper takes a chunk out of her. And each time, the creature that she saved offers up a piece of itself as a replacement for the Wizened's lost piece of flesh. Eventually, the Wizened is a patchwork of all the woodland creatures the Keeper likes to torture, which is why they can inspire the entire forest to revolt against the Keeper, saving everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:24:01-07:00","id":574787,"title":"","content":"I always thought changeling was of the most brilliant creative and original games i've ever read,and holy nuggets,David really is enhacing the things that made the game amazimg,this edition is going to blow peoples minds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:27:49-07:00","id":574793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574783#post574783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you put it that way, I agree with you. That character would only show up on Earth as a Loyalist.<br /> <br /> But, I think you're missing part of the point of the Seeming. It sounds like part of the point of the Wizened is that their Durance in Arcadia was both emotionally and physically damaging to them. Even if they were taken to do the stuff they love doing, either the nature of the place or their perception of it prevents them from being truly fulfilled there.<br /> <br /> Also, just because they were taken to use their special skill doesn't mean that the Keeper wants to use it in a way that the proto-Wizened will enjoy. For example, coming back to our Truefriend, maybe the person was taken because she was good with animals and just really, really liked them. As such, she's taken by a sadistic Keeper, who likes to watch her try to stop him from torturing other creatures. Each time she successfully interposes herself between the Keeper and his prey, the Keeper takes a chunk out of her. And each time, the creature that she saved offers up a piece of itself as a replacement for the Wizened's lost piece of flesh. Eventually, the Wizened is a patchwork of all the woodland creatures the Keeper likes to torture, which is why they can inspire the entire forest to revolt against the Keeper, saving everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a really cool character concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:50:39-07:00","id":574809,"title":"","content":"I think Charlaquin's notion highlights an important point: the Seemings only apply to changelings who end up escaping from Arcadia. It's entirely possible for someone to go to Arcadia and find that he fits in there perfectly, and so never bothers to even attempt to escape. But he's not who <b>Changeling</b> is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:52:57-07:00","id":574811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574720#post574720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I haven't made it clear; the Seemings have all been sort of... format spitballing? I'm considering a few different routes here. I'm leaning toward:<br /> <br /> Benefits:<br /> <br /> 1) Coping mechanism/Clarity gain thing.<br /> <br /> 2) A mechanical boost to your escape thing.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) A thing that risks Clarity, adds to your list of risks.<br /> <br /> 2) A thing that makes your Changeling experience a little more complicated mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as spitballing goes, this feels pretty solid; what defines you and what puts that at risk are good cores for the whole &quot;Claiming your identity&quot; aspect. The issue that concerns me is the mechanical boosts, because mechanics help give definition to characterization if absolutely nothing else.<br /> <br /> It's somewhat easier to do penalties than benefits, because penalties take away from a universal, so the characters don't gain specialization in a particular area. The Beast penalty, for example, of having a harder time slipping manacles won't limit the number of potential Beast escape artists. Frankly, the opposite is more likely. In the end, it doesn't mechanically incentivize <i>one</i> kind of Beast. A mechanical benefit of some sort encourages a particular field of endeavour, and people won't really slot that into place if it doesn't aid the character's area of focus.<br /> <br /> It's something to think carefully on. For the Wizened, I think this is well done, because what their creative endeavour <i>is</i> doesn't have broad limits. A Wizened who acts as the alderman for a freehold may spend their time better organizing its affairs. One with a more social bent might take time to write a speech. Ultimately, the benefit is tied into the concept of the Wizened's self-definition, rather than defining them in a specific way.<br /> <br /> Not sure if this is helpful or something you have long since considered but, with 1e, if you wanted to play a social character, you played a Fairest. If you played an Elemental or a Wizened, you put yourself at a disadvantage when doing social characters. 2e looks to be trying to avoid this and I sincerely hope it manages it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:58:32-07:00","id":574814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574809#post574809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Charlaquin's notion highlights an important point: the Seemings only apply to changelings who end up escaping from Arcadia. It's entirely possible for someone to go to Arcadia and find that he fits in there perfectly, and so never bothers to even attempt to escape. But he's not who <b>Changeling</b> is about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget about Changelings who were rescued by other Changelings? They are free and ostensibly happy to be out of Arcadia, but would not have a Seeming because they did not have the strength or foresight to escape. This would also be true about privateers, who are not always recognized as such among other Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:01:06-07:00","id":574817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574814#post574814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget about Changelings who were rescued by other Changelings? They are free and ostensibly happy to be out of Arcadia, but would not have a Seeming because they did not have the strength or foresight to escape. This would also be true about privateers, who are not always recognized as such among other Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which begs the question of how they escaped.<br /> <br /> Although didn't 1e have a &quot;it has to be a conscious choice&quot; thing? You needed memories of home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:07:38-07:00","id":574818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574817#post574817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although didn't 1e have a &quot;it has to be a conscious choice&quot; thing? You needed memories of home.</div> </div> </div> </div>You needed memories of home to find your way home, not to get through the Hedge at all. Getting out on the coattails of another fugitive was still a thing and it had just as much of an impact on how other changelings who knew of it were likely to view your probable loyalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:07:41-07:00","id":574819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574781#post574781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible to be passionate about an art, to find oneself supernaturally augmented to carry it out, and still find it hollow and unsatisfying in Arcadia's climate. Never mind that an atmosphere to freely practice an art is one thing, and an atmosphere to practice an art while one of the Gentry waits to be impressed is quite another. &quot;As long as I'm here, I can't express myself, not really. Because if I don't express myself exactly the way my Keeper wants today... Ohh, no, no, no. I can't let myself think of what he'll do to me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I also keep thinking of <i>The Snow Queen </i>by Mercedes Lackey. Briefly, the setting is a fantasy kingdom inspired by Scandanavia (well this book is anyway) where the magic causes Stories and fairy tales to keep happening and the various Fairy Godmothers try to keep them from ruining people's lives in the process. The B plot for the book is that has spotted a boy who is likely to turn into a Clockwork Artisan (and, in this particular case, a likely serial killer) so, she's invoked the story of the Snow Queen and taken him off to her palace and given him everything he thought he wanted: workshops, tools, libraries, whatever he might need to create amazing things ...but she's also ensured that he can't see any of the servants, she personally remains cold and aloof when he's around, so he no longer has any of the adulation or praise that he thinks is due him, just all the space he needs to realize that what he really, really wants is not to be alone anymore.<br /> <br /> The nature of that particular series is such that he gets a happy ending with his true love, because that's what the Godmother wanted, but I could easily see a non-altruistic Keeper grabbing someone who complains about not having the time or space to Create, giving them everything they asked for, which only shows them that what they really want is companionship or something. Said person won't necessarily wind up Wizened (they might be Fairest or something actually), but it nicely illustrates the problems that can ensue when an alien entity tries to give a human what it thinks is the human's heart's desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:09:33-07:00","id":574820,"title":"","content":"On the Wizened Seeming: I think I just fell in love. <br /> <br /> \u201cArt\u201d isn't a matter of what you do, but how you do it. The cook in a MASH unit isn't an artist; he can't afford to be, as he has the much more important responsibility of ensuring that everybody gets fed in a timely manner. OTOH, a chef on a luxury liner can use the same skills to prepare a meal that his patrons would die for \u2014 or kill for. Both are cooks; but one is concerned about quantity over quality, and the other is concerned with achieving excellence in his chosen profession. The Wizened is a would-be chef who's forced to prepare meals for a MASH unit day in and day out, until he finally finds a way to achieve greatness even under those conditions by tossing away everything that isn't part of the finely honed chef he wishes to become. <br /> <br /> I think it's also worth noting that just about anything can be an art. There's a reason why fighting styles of the orient are so often referred to as \u201cmartial arts\u201d; parkour can also be thought of as an art. And then there's the art of the deal. As long as what you're doing is done with style, it's an art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:20:46-07:00","id":574824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574814#post574814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget about Changelings who were rescued by other Changelings? They are free and ostensibly happy to be out of Arcadia, but would not have a Seeming because they did not have the strength or foresight to escape. This would also be true about privateers, who are not always recognized as such among other Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; there are potentially changelings without Seemings. But that wasn't my point; my point is that people who don't want to escape will never get Seemings: Seemings are only for those who wish to leave Arcadia. And thus Seeming write-ups will only reflect Durances that are in some way uncomfortable or unsatisfying. There may well be many a craftsman who is taken to Arcadia and put to work, and who loves it and never leaves. They will never be Wizened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T23:43:28-07:00","id":574830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574820#post574820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Wizened Seeming: I think I just fell in love.<br /> <br /> \u201cArt\u201d isn't a matter of what you do, but how you do it. The cook in a MASH unit isn't an artist; he can't afford to be, as he has the much more important responsibility of ensuring that everybody gets fed in a timely manner. OTOH, a chef on a luxury liner can use the same skills to prepare a meal that his patrons would die for \u2014 or kill for. Both are cooks; but one is concerned about quantity over quality, and the other is concerned with achieving excellence in his chosen profession. The Wizened is a would-be chef who's forced to prepare meals for a MASH unit day in and day out, until he finally finds a way to achieve greatness even under those conditions by tossing away everything that isn't part of the finely honed chef he wishes to become.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth noting that just about anything can be an art. There's a reason why fighting styles of the orient are so often referred to as \u201cmartial arts\u201d; parkour can also be thought of as an art. And then there's the art of the deal. As long as what you're doing is done with style, it's an art.</div> </div> </div> </div>....And now I'm thinking about Charles Emerson Winchester III, who was a doctor at a MASH unit, instead of a cook, but they had a similar &quot;do it quick, not pretty&quot; approach to surgery too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T00:09:09-07:00","id":574841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574732#post574732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if their thing was being a good friend before they were taken, and they were taken to be a good friend, they would not feel the emptiness of not being able to do their thing during their durance that causes one to become a Wizened. They would probably just stay in Arcadia, happy to finally find a place where they are completely fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I don't like about the new seemings; the idea that certain backgrounds/Durances lead to escapes and others don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T00:39:04-07:00","id":574866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574841#post574841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I don't like about the new seemings; the idea that certain backgrounds/Durances lead to escapes and others don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... Our experiences shape who we become later in life. Certain backgrounds lead to certain career paths and others don't. Why should Seemings be different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T00:40:54-07:00","id":574867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574841#post574841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I don't like about the new seemings; the idea that certain backgrounds/Durances lead to escapes and others don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certain kinds of people are more likely to take certain paths to freedom. I'm not sure why that's a particularly controversial concept. I don't believe making Seemings feel more arbitrary will be beneficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T02:12:40-07:00","id":574915,"title":"","content":"Once again, I don't like this fix idea that characters BEFORE their durance must've had a certain personality/behaviour. It limits freedom rather than enhance it. If it is intended to be that it's <u>common</u> amongst wizened to be loner artists rather than the rule, then it should be more clear in the text.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the clarity breaking point is just bonkers. Is a changeling wizened with 7-9 dices ever going to fail their crafts roll, possibly boosted up by Good tools +2 and other stuffs? Make it eaiser to fuck it up. For instance, demand 2 successes rather than one because they seek perfection and would be unhappy with a &quot;shoddy&quot; performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T02:35:55-07:00","id":574927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574915#post574915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, the clarity breaking point is just bonkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574915#post574915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, I don't like this fix idea that characters BEFORE their durance must've had a certain personality/behaviour. It limits freedom rather than enhance it. If it is intended to be that it's <u>common</u> amongst wizened to be loner artists rather than the rule, then it should be more clear in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if it's not clear enough to you that the description is an iconic example, and you can differ from that. However, I should probably note that we focus on iconic examples in almost every OPP product's core splat description, and this has been doubly so since we started Second Edition. I'm not going to genericize text just so you're more comfortable deviating from the stereotype. I wouldn't tell you &quot;Ventrue are sometimes domineering. But not always, because they don't have to be. Sometimes they are. Some are also quite weak-willed. Some are even submissive. Most are domineering. But please don't interpret 'most' as 'all', because that's not the case.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is doubly the case because we've went out of our way to NOT indicate in the concept examples that they have to be a certain way prior to their Durances. I can try to make this a little less subtle in the final draft. But I'm not going to make it significantly less subtle. I'll also include an explicit clause in the Seeming chapter opening that states the listed introductions are just evocative, iconic examples, and should not be taken as gospel for every single character. That you are allowed doing something different from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T02:56:48-07:00","id":574942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574927#post574927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean for it to come out as offenssive, if that is what you are trying to imply. I apologize, English is not my first language and I thought bonkers was a rather 'kind' word to use when explaining something that you thought didn't work out.<br /> It is way to easy to -not- hit your clarity breaking point was my point, not to call you or whoever came up with the idea unintelligent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574927#post574927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if it's not clear enough t\u0336o\u0336 \u0336y\u0336o\u0336u\u0336 that the description is an iconic example, and you can differ from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There, fixed it for you!<br /> If something is misinterpreted, please keep in mind that in nine cases out of ten, it's the person trying to communicate that message who done messed up rather than the listener &quot;not getting it&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it's not about it being less subtle, it's about the first edition books going out of their way NOT to create stereotypes and here it seems to be the norm. The idea of creating a clause prior to the seeming descriptions seems brilliant, just what I wanted! :3<br /> <br /> Additionally, now that I have your attention for a few moments, I earlier made a thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\">concerning the apperance of changelings</a>. Care to give me your thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T03:17:26-07:00","id":574960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574942#post574942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There, fixed it for you!<br /> If something is misinterpreted, please keep in mind that in nine cases out of ten, it's the person trying to communicate that message who done messed up rather than the listener &quot;not getting it&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, this point has come up a number of times now. Every time, someone different comes in and explains exactly what I'm saying right now: These are iconic examples. Your characters do not have to skew to the example. Then, I explain that I'll make it clearer in the final draft. Example-driven presentation has been a White Wolf/CCP/Onyx Path staple for a very long time. But I will make an explicit statement that examples do not constitute 100% representation. I may even bold the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T04:02:23-07:00","id":574979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574960#post574960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool!<br /> So what did you think of the thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\">concerning the apperance of changelings</a>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T04:09:06-07:00","id":574984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574979#post574979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool!<br /> So what did you think of the thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be\">concerning the apperance of changelings</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:09:01-07:00","id":575054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574820#post574820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's also worth noting that just about anything can be an art. There's a reason why fighting styles of the orient are so often referred to as \u201cmartial arts\u201d; parkour can also be thought of as an art. And then there's the art of the deal. As long as what you're doing is done with style, it's an art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idea! A young Changeling, maybe 15-18, takes up acrobatics and free running to escape the massive arguments his parents have been having recently. When a Keeper appears to offer him a place to run without ceasing he initially accepts. Later, however, he realizes all he really wanted was for his parents to stop fighting, and gives himself over to the motion in order to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:30:08-07:00","id":575080,"title":"","content":"The Wizened of 2e = Stanley Gimble<br /> <br /> Guy's so obsessed with prosthetics he gives himself one for the sole purpose of enhancing his awareness of how they should be crafted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23rQnX_trIU\" data-code=\"23rQnX_trIU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/23rQnX_trIU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T06:07:04-07:00","id":575107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574728#post574728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes, but that is still something that an autistic person can relate to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really dig that you feel that way. Talking to Filamena, I know it's a thing that was on her mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:30:03-07:00","id":575187,"title":"","content":"Soldier Kith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:39:15-07:00","id":575192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=575187#post575187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soldier Kith?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forearms replaced with assault rifles, cigar clenched in his teeth, cranium replaced with a marine helmet, and twin grenade bandoleers sewed to his chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-01-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:00:13-07:00","id":575228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=575080#post575080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wizened of 2e = Stanley Gimble<br /> <br /> Guy's so obsessed with prosthetics he gives himself one for the sole purpose of enhancing his awareness of how they should be crafted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=23rQnX_trIU\" data-code=\"23rQnX_trIU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/23rQnX_trIU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>There is also Kimiko Ross, who in the latest Dresden Codak, does this to herself: <a href=\"http://dresdencodak.com/2015/06/15/dark-science-48-final-form/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dresdencodak.com/2015/06/15/d...48-final-form/</a> (Kim has been replacing parts of herself since the beginning of the comic, including some casual DNA tinkering, so by itself, this one comic really isn't much of a spoiler.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:10:48-07:00","id":575239,"title":"","content":"As a note guys, remembering that the point of the discussion is not to beat a dead horse. I know we love making carcass paste, I indulge in it myself on occasion, but it's really not the point. Focus on new concerns, look beyond the trends.<br /> <br /> Focusing on the trends you find problematic means you miss out on elements specific to the Seeming, which can use preening as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:40:32-07:00","id":575274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574614#post574614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off of this, Wizened are coming off a lot more like Elementals from First edition, with physically incorporating things into them. I'm also finding it a bit hard to see how they've escaped... it feels like they're damaged in their time in Arcadia, so they make do by sowing themselves back up with whatever things that are around, but that doesn't seem to lead into the choice to escape that the new Seemings are attempting to do, as it feels like what they've been doing in Arcadia already.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know what you mean. I have a 1e character who was made as an iconic Elemental, but with the 2e Seemings he actually feels more like a Wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T09:14:27-07:00","id":575289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574729#post574729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that some examples of possible Durances for each Seeming would be nice, because I'm having a tough time visualizing how this would work or how rebuilding themselves with their tools helps them escape. Despite, yes, getting that both Iron Man and Nick Chopper are Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd welcome this. The same goes for all the Seemings, frankly, but I also just tend to feel like I need a lot of examples to really &quot;get&quot; something. &gt;.&gt; More points help me triangulate. I'd certainly find them more useful than the Concepts, which... honestly, don't feel like they give me much I hadn't already gotten from reading the Seeming write-up and the Seeming-specific Kith manifestations. &quot;How this happened&quot; examples seem more helpful to me than &quot;end result&quot; examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly this is just my own bias, but this seems a bit focused on creators and makers, people who make physical things or who create art, but it seems like you could also do, say, a Wizened Truefriend who's thing was empathy and helping you out ...to the point that they completely ignore their own needs because they're too focused on the stuff they're doing for their Motley. And I'm not entirely sure that comes across in the text. </div> </div> </div>I very much like this character idea, and I agree with your point. No doubt physical creators and practitioners of more conventional art forms would be very common, granted, but stuff like this example wouldn't have occurred to me in the current draft. It really feels to me like it opens up the Seeming a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T10:06:56-07:00","id":575310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574867#post574867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain kinds of people are more likely to take certain paths to freedom. I'm not sure why that's a particularly controversial concept. I don't believe making Seemings feel more arbitrary will be beneficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really quite simple. I feel that who you were before your durance should be about 30% of the influence on your eventual seeming; with the form of your durance and whatever escape oppotunities present themselves being the other 70%. The current write up feels more like it's 90% background.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to go into detail what exactly gives me the impression it's 90% - even though I know it's supposed to be an iconic example. But I know you're getting frustraited with this coming up repeatedly so I won't unless you ask me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574867#post574867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe making Seemings feel more arbitrary will be beneficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not suggesting they become more arbitrary. What I want to see is to honour the internal logic of the setting.<br /> <br /> Your Seeming is chosen by the method in which you escape. That's going to depend upon a lot of factors: Form of your durance, escape opportunities, personality of keeper, and yes - your personality. I don't think it's arbitary to say that, e.g. having the Maker or Artist Kith is going to significantly increase the odds of you becoming Wizened because you quickly acquire useful skills and encounter Wizened-appropriate escape opportunities.<br /> <br /> Basically I dislike the feeling that Seeming is 90% a Changeling's pre-Durance background <i>precisely</i> <i>because</i> it clashes with the setting's internal logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574867#post574867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also include an explicit clause in the Seeming chapter opening that states the listed introductions are just evocative, iconic examples, and should not be taken as gospel for every single character. That you are allowed doing something different from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad to hear that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574866#post574866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... Our experiences shape who we become later in life. Certain backgrounds lead to certain career paths and others don't. Why should Seemings be different?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because Seemings <i>are</i> fundamentally different from career paths.<br /> <br /> A career path is typically chosen after plenty of thoght; with many oppotunities to change your mind. Your Seeming comes from one single decision that's made in extreme circumstances that marks you for the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> In my estimation those extreme circumstances mean that a lot of Changelings would end up with a Seeming that's mostly unrelated to who they were before hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-01-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T11:03:38-07:00","id":575358,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in hearing specifically why you feel the background makes up 90% of the deciding factor, but I also don't want to fill up dozens of pages of this thread with it like we did in the Darkling thread. Would you care to discuss it in messages, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T11:29:43-07:00","id":575376,"title":"","content":"Sure. Expect a PM soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T11:48:20-07:00","id":575413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=575358#post575358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be interested in hearing specifically why you feel the background makes up 90% of the deciding factor, but I also don't want to fill up dozens of pages of this thread with it like we did in the Darkling thread. Would you care to discuss it in messages, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=575376#post575376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Expect a PM soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in this line of discussions as well, and suspect I'm not alone. I don't mean to come off as nosy, but if you two wouldn't be opposed, how does starting a new thread on the topic sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T12:15:25-07:00","id":575464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=575413#post575413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in this line of discussions as well, and suspect I'm not alone. I don't mean to come off as nosy, but if you two wouldn't be opposed, how does starting a new thread on the topic sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be fine with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T12:28:00-07:00","id":575467,"title":"","content":"I'll copy my PM into a new thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T14:04:16-07:00","id":575599,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Well, that settles it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">I'm playing a Wizened investigator ala Sherlock Holmes (possibly closer to the </span><i>Elementary</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> version with a few nods towards RDJ's portrayal)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T14:44:14-07:00","id":575669,"title":"","content":"The curse feels a bit simplistic to me. The definition of failure is a bit narrow and I feel like I'm kind of forced into playing someone who's not an absolute expert in their craft if I want it to still be relevant (and I like playing people who are good at one thing and one thing only). Imagine a kind of composer, who was a gentry's twisted vision of what a court composer should be. I'm not talking music student who took composition as a side project. I'm talking Bach levels of &quot;this is what I do&quot;. Now it's not completely unreasonable such person would roll close to 10 dice when composing a symphony. Her chances for failure are abysmal, so the curse will almost never be a problem. But let's say she gets 1 success. The piece is competent. It doesn't have any blatant mistake, and some might say it's good. But according to her standards, it's really not. The theme might be a bit stale, this part might be a bit too long, that one poorly orchestrated, some tasteless harmonies here and there. So even if it was a mechanical success, for her it was a failure because the problem with perfection, is that the better you are at something, the bigger your expectations get.<br /> <br /> Now I've seen many artists who are perfectly fine with their mediocrity, in fact I'd say that's sadly most artists, but to me those people are not really Wizened. The &quot;Wizened type&quot; artists I know (and I would include myself in there if it wasn't utterly pretentious), as in people who are the thing that they do, all suffer from the &quot;everything I do is shit&quot; syndrome. Not that they can't be ever satisfied with what they do, but to them &quot;success&quot; and &quot;failure&quot; have different meanings. Also I talk about artists because I'm a musician and that's the field I know, but I'm pretty sure it can apply to anything a Wizened could be.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that I'd like it to either not be that mechanical like : &quot;anytime your character considers the result of a roll related to her art a failure, clarity breaking point&quot; with a loose guideline of how much successes would be considered a true success based on your dicepool. Or have some mechanic hardcode that hole &quot;perceived failure&quot; thing, like &quot;anytime you roll less successes than half the amount of points you have in the skill needed to perform your art, you suffer a clarity breaking point&quot;. Something like that could also make some experts but not so clever changelings realize that they are reaching the end of their capacity (high skill low attributes means that you have high expectations for yourself but perhaps don't have the capacity to carry it out) or alternatively they could spend points of willpower anytime they practice their art which would make very very dedicated artists, or they could altogether stop because it hurts too much, and recovering the simple capacity of trying might be an arc in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6219-kzz","name":"kzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T16:40:56-07:00","id":575767,"title":"","content":"Heh. \u201cI'm a perfectionist! Anything less than an exceptional success is a failure in my eyes!&quot; Mechanically, that might be a bit much: on the one hand, you only need to achieve three successes to get an exceptional success because of your Blessing; but on the other hand, how often do even <i>three</i> successes come up on a dice pool? Maybe the rule could be that if you don't get multiple successes on a roll pertaining to your craft, your efforts weren't good enough for you and you suffer a Breaking Point. <br /> <br /> Or how about this as a radically different approach (possibly too radical): if you invest Glamour into a roll pertaining to your craft, you set a bar of one success per point of Glamour invested. If you achieve that many successes, you get one more success per point of Glamour invested; but if you don't reach that threshold, you suffer an &quot;inadequate performance\u201d breaking point at a penalty equal to the amount of Glamour you invested \u2014 you still get the successes that you rolled, but they weren't good enough for your own perfectionist standards. As soon as you invest Glamour in your craft, you're committed: either you'll achieve a spectacular result or you'll crash and burn \u2014 and the more Glamour you invest, the more spectacular the result, one way or the other. <br /> <br /> If that's too radical for an innate Seeming power, maybe it could be a Seeming Contract somewhere\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T19:15:28-07:00","id":575906,"title":"","content":"Wizened have gone from my least favorite seeming, to one I would actually consider playing.<br /> <br /> Now that I've seen all of them, I appear to have gone from.<br /> <br /> Wizened &lt; Ogres &lt; Fairest &lt; Darklings &lt; Beasts &lt; Elementals<br /> <br /> to<br /> <br /> Fairest &lt; Ogres &lt;Elementals &lt; Wizened &lt; Darklings &lt; Beasts<br /> <br /> not entirely accurate to my feelings, but I think it gets the point across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:11:16-07:00","id":576001,"title":"","content":"I think that the Curse is fine. Two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Frequency - Wizened will likely be making this roll a lot. Even with a low chance of failure, you roll often enough and you're going to fail occasionally.<br /> <br /> 2. Negative modifiers - Have a crazy high dice pool, but want to make your curse relevant? Challenge yourself and accumulate negative modifiers. Work faster, with poorer tools, in adverse conditions. Parkour expert? Do it in the rain. Blindfolded. World class sculptor? Make your next sculpture out of butterfly wings. In a wind storm. Great painter? Paint a hyper-realistic portrait with no reference. In an hour. With crayons. People who are as passionate and driven as the Wizened are always pushing themselves. Sometimes to an insane degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:14:22-07:00","id":576008,"title":"","content":"I would like to voice my support for the blessings and curses having both a clarity effect and a minor mechanical effect. I'm happy to hear that this is still being tweaked; I was a little worried they were going to be inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:42:05-07:00","id":576023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576001#post576001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Curse is fine. Two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Frequency - Wizened will likely be making this roll a lot. Even with a low chance of failure, you roll often enough and you're going to fail occasionally.<br /> <br /> 2. Negative modifiers - Have a crazy high dice pool, but want to make your curse relevant? Challenge yourself and accumulate negative modifiers. Work faster, with poorer tools, in adverse conditions. Parkour expert? Do it in the rain. Blindfolded. World class sculptor? Make your next sculpture out of butterfly wings. In a wind storm. Great painter? Paint a hyper-realistic portrait with no reference. In an hour. With crayons. People who are as passionate and driven as the Wizened are always pushing themselves. Sometimes to an insane degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think negative modifiers are something a lot of people under-use. I love them. I use them constantly. I'm pretty much of a mind that without negatives, most things aren't worth rolling. That's sort of a function of the Storytelling System so heavily favouring success, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:48:32-07:00","id":576024,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, negative (and positive!) modifiers are hard to use because half the time I forget they exist. I know from my 1.0 Changeling game, players started doing them more often when I gave them their contract example modifiers on their sheets as a bit of a quick reference of how to influence things.<br /> <br /> They also get excessively fiddly in a LARP situation which I played a lot (so for the most part they're ignored), but considering MET stuff isn't handled by OP that's pretty understandable nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:49:01-07:00","id":576071,"title":"","content":"I might add a once per scene limit to the curse, actually. Somebody brought up a martial arts wizened as a possibility, and it occurred to me that Defense can get pretty high, meaning that in a combat with worthy opponents the aforementioned martial arts wizened might fail several attack rolls, even if he ends up winning the fight. I don't think I'd want to make their player roll a breaking point each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T23:03:21-07:00","id":576080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576071#post576071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might add a once per scene limit to the curse, actually. Somebody brought up a martial arts wizened as a possibility, and it occurred to me that Defense can get pretty high, meaning that in a combat with worthy opponents the aforementioned martial arts wizened might fail several attack rolls, even if he ends up winning the fight. I don't think I'd want to make their player roll a breaking point each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking Points are going to be one per scene. You take the worst, then modify it if there should be a bunch of them. I hate rolling over and over for that sort of stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T06:07:02-07:00","id":576293,"title":"","content":"I'm really torn on this 2ED Wizened. I <b>really</b> love this &quot;<i>I'm genius!</i>&quot; attitude they have about chosen Art and as a means of escape. But I'm putted of by the whole &quot;...I replace mine body parts for it&quot;. I can agree some ideas can could work this &quot;<i>Terminator</i>-like ascetic&quot;, but I'm do not see this as very much Fairy Tale motive and working counter to idea of 1ED Wizened - where you work so hard for the Keeper you were diminished, literally.<br /> <br /> I still want to have mine <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwarf_(Germanic_mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">dwarven</a> craftsmen from <b><i>R</i></b><i><b>ing of the Nibelung</b></i>, elvish Santa Claus helpers and mouse-humans making Cinderella Pumpkin Carrie. Now I will get only <i>Robocop</i> wannabes, throwing away their human parts instead of becoming more and more tired and used in work process. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-02-2015, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T08:08:17-07:00","id":576374,"title":"","content":"Look through the sample Kiths, and note what being Wizened does to them. For all the Seeming's talk about becoming a workaholic cyborg, the actual effect still seems to lean more toward diminutive stature and the like. Not always, thankfully; but often enough that I don't think the classic image of a Wizened is going away any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T08:35:59-07:00","id":576393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576374#post576374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look through the sample Kiths, and note what being Wizened does to them. For all the Seeming's talk about becoming a workaholic cyborg, the actual effect still seems to lean more toward diminutive stature and the like. Not always, thankfully; but often enough that I don't think the classic image of a Wizened is going away any time soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just did look through them, and that's simply untrue.<br /> <br /> Here are all 16 of the ones from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\">the sample</a>. Every single Kith association emphasizes the artificial nature of the changes. A reduction in size or stature is simply not mentioned in any of them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kiths Sample Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Antiquarian</b><br /> - Wizened: Their eyes have built in jeweler's loups and their hands contain precise clockwork gears. They are a melding of centuries old technology and grey, slightly dusty flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Artist</b><br /> - Wizened: This creature has been altered to best perform its favored form of art. Its fingers have been given additional joints and its entire body now seems optimized for drawing, woodworking, or whatever other art is most often performs.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimera</b><br /> - Wizened: At least three different creatures appear to have been grafted together in a scarred Frankenstein-like assembly.<br /> <br /> <b>Draconic</b><br /> - Wizened: They are clearly a human who has been remade into a dragon, with human eyes and the forms of human limbs beneath their scales.<br /> <br /> <b>Fireheart</b><br /> - Wizened: Crystal bands glowing with flickering internal fire are grafted to the creature's joints. When it becomes emotional, fire briefly engulfs its head or hands before the crystals suppress it.<br /> <br /> <b>Grey</b><br /> - Wizened: Their grey hairless skin has been fitted small implants made of metal and glowing glass, especially around their enlarged skulls.<br /> <br /> <b>Leechfinger</b><br /> - Wizened: Narrow tubes radiating from their heart run along the surface of the skin of their arms and torso. These tubes connect to fine needles under their fingernails and in bands around their wrists.<br /> <br /> <b>Lurker</b><br /> - Wizened: Extra fingers and joints have been grafted onto their hands and wires that help speed their reactions run along the surface of their arms.<br /> <br /> <b>Maniken</b><br /> - Wizened: Although no trace of flesh remains, it's clear that this construct of brushed aluminum, colored wires, and advanced circuits was made by replacing portions of a human body one piece at a time.<br /> <br /> <b>Metalflesh</b><br /> - Wizened: Welded and riveted plates of bronze fit around what was once a human body, but which may no longer exist beneath the metal.<br /> <br /> <b>Oracle</b><br /> - Wizened: All have a third, obviously inhuman or artificial eye in the middle of their forehead.<br /> <br /> <b>Palewraith</b><br /> - Wizened: Clearly artificial transparent plastic skin stretched over oddly pale organs and muscles.<br /> <br /> <b>Sandharrowed</b><br /> - Wizened: A creature made of shifting sand stabilized by narrow glowing metal and glass bands at its major joints.<br /> <br /> <b>Smith</b><br /> - Wizened: Their powerful corded muscles and strong hands are augmented by metal cables running along their arms and tools replacing some of their fingers.<br /> <br /> <b>Telluric</b><br /> - Wizened: Its large eyes look like swirling galaxies and are obvious artificial, as are the thin onyx plates attached to its skin with shining silver rivets.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Becoming smaller is plausible, as part of making the Wizened better at whatever her art is, but it doesn't feature in any of the examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:20:56-07:00","id":576456,"title":"","content":"I mean, there had to be some kind of change to Wizened with the new Seeming Paradigm. In 1e they were entirely defined by the task their Keeper made them do. In 2e, that's the role of Kiths, not Seemings. In order to preserve the &quot;expert artisan&quot; identity, the character's art had to become the way they changed themselves to escape, instead of the way their Keeper changed them to suit their role. The transhuman asthetic they've got going on is a natural extension of that; they modified their own bodies so they could perfect their trade and use that to reclaim agency.<br /> <br /> Personally, I still see the shriveled aspect in the new Wizened, it's just less literal. Instead of being physically shrunken, it's their humanity that's been diminished. The Wizened doesn't make herself a <i>smaller person</i>, she makes herself <i>less of a person</i>. They sacrifice their bodies to become the perfect form for creating their art. <br /> <br /> That's also the answer to the question of &quot;what did the Wizened give up&quot;, by the way. They gave up their humanity. They chose to stop being an imperfect <i>being</i> and become a perfect <i>tool</i> instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-02-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:37:47-07:00","id":576517,"title":"","content":"Not that Arcadia ever treats metaphors and wordplay as simply that. Making ones self less of a person is bound to actually physically diminish one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:39:00-07:00","id":576520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576517#post576517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that Arcadia ever treats metaphors and wordplay as simply that. Making ones self less of a person is bound to actually physically diminish one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, which means the literal diminutive aspect is not gone if you want it to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:39:11-07:00","id":576521,"title":"","content":"My issue with the appearance, is that I just don't think it's visually appealing. A doctor with scalpels for fingers doesn't say &quot;the best doctor ever&quot; to me. It says &quot;psychotic serial killer&quot; (and also &quot;how does he tie his shoelaces?&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-02-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:04:28-07:00","id":576535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576521#post576521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with the appearance, is that I just don't think it's visually appealing. A doctor with scalpels for fingers doesn't say &amp;quot;the best doctor ever&amp;quot; to me. It says &amp;quot;psychotic serial killer&amp;quot; (and also &amp;quot;how does he tie his shoelaces?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't have to be a doctor with scalpels for fingers. Maybe he has extra joints in his fingers to perform surgery more nimbly. Maybe he has pockets built into his skin to carry extra tools in. Maybe one or both of his eyes has a built-in telescopic magnifying lense so he can focus his attention on smaller details when he needs to, or see the big picture when that's more pertinent. Maybe he has additional functioning limbs grafted onto his body (mechanical or organic, I'd say that's a matter of preference) so he can perform multiple tasks simultaneously. There are plenty of ways you can visually express the idea of a transhuman being who has integrated the tools of his trade into his own body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:29:22-07:00","id":576557,"title":"","content":"Sort of. The problem to me is &quot;integrated the tools of his trade into his own body&quot;. A lot of your ideas are not &quot;the tools of his trade&quot; but generically useful. Extra jointed fingers, that could be piano player as easily as a surgeon. Magnifying eyes, surgeon, artist, jeweler, I could go on.<br /> <br /> The thing is that, from a practical transhumanism point of view, why on earth would you integrate the tools of your trade into your body? Replacing your arms with superior robotic arms; sure. But what advantage does a biologically integrated scalpel have over a scalpel you hold in your hands? When transhumanism starts going impractical like that, I stop thinking autistic savant and start thinking Batman villian.<br /> <br /> I think Wizened always looking like they've just finished at 16 hour shift would capture the Seeming's themes better than built in tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-02-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:42:56-07:00","id":576569,"title":"","content":"*shrug* I figure there will be a fair bit of visual overlap between Wizend of different Kiths. Point is, they don't just make themselves better at their craft, they make themselves part of their craft. A Wizend Artist is as much art as artisan. A Wizened Antiquarian is as much antique as curator. A Wizened Oracle is as much prophecy as prophet. However you feel best visually represents that should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:51:33-07:00","id":576590,"title":"","content":"If a Wizened Artist is also Art, then they <a href=\"http://www.dorkadia.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/CelShadeMakeup.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">should look like a painting</a>, not have paintbrush fingers.<br /> <br /> (Also, your craft need not be related to your Kith)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:59:03-07:00","id":576609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576590#post576590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Wizened Artist is also Art, then they <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dorkadia.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/CelShadeMakeup.jpg&amp;quot;]should</a> look like a painting[/URL], not have paintbrush fingers.<br /> <br /> (Also, your craft need not be related to your Kith)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant art as in the process of creating art, not as in a work of art. The latter would be more Elemental territory. And you are correct, the Wizend's craft (and their modifications) need not be directly related to their Kith, I was just using Kiths as examples.<br /> Also, I would probably give a Wizened artist something like a built-in pallet than brush fingers. Maybe brush-like fingernails, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:02:07-07:00","id":576618,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://s3.amazonaws.com/rapgenius/1363126452_taco-girl-meme-generator-why-not-both-6ec00b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Just saying.<br /> <br /> To borrow from Mummy, sometimes the Verse Speaks Itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:54:03-07:00","id":576647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576609#post576609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I would probably give a Wizened artist something like a built-in pallet than brush fingers. Maybe brush-like fingernails, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still feels more like a Batman villian than someone who's really into their craft.<br /> <br /> Though I still really like the idea of a Wizened artist being part painting. They retreat into their craft not just metaphorically but literally. Painting over the scars when their Keeper beats them. Well sort of; they might not do it before their Escape; but once they became Wizened they retroactively did so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T12:07:29-07:00","id":576652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576647#post576647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still feels more like a Batman villian than someone who's really into their craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576647#post576647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I still really like the idea of a Wizened artist being part painting. They retreat into their craft not just metaphorically but literally. Painting over the scars when their Keeper beats them. Well sort of; they might not do it before their Escape; but once they became Wizened they retroactively did so.</div> </div> </div> </div>that does sound pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T13:12:04-07:00","id":576692,"title":"","content":"I agree with almost all the <b>King's Raven</b> say - I <b>am</b> the transhumanist and all I see in Wizened Kiths example is bad &quot;I replaced my limbs for tools&quot;. It may work in pulpish <i>Evil Dead</i>, but not in the Fairy Tale about people stolen by &quot;Evil Elves&quot; and taking they way out of it, on their own rules.<br /> <br /> I did not thought I will write it ever, but I disagree with <b>Charlaquin</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576456#post576456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there had to be some kind of change to Wizened with the new Seeming Paradigm. In 1e they were entirely defined by the task their Keeper made them do. In 2e, that's the role of Kiths, not Seemings. In order to preserve the &quot;expert artisan&quot; identity, the character's art had to become the way they changed themselves to escape, instead of the way their Keeper changed them to suit their role. The transhuman asthetic they've got going on is a natural extension of that; they modified their own bodies so they could perfect their trade and use that to reclaim agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why cannot it be &quot;I spent next 39 years working tirelessly to take off the shakcles between working at Keepers worhshop&quot; it was in the 1ED, without &quot;bad transhumainism&quot; elements? It <b>is</b> Agancy - <i>I work so much to free myself, I lost years of life</i> - buy &quot;overworked and diminished&quot; is somehow bad ascetics?<br /> <br /> <b>To me &quot;I broke my all bones and had rough skin from overwork&quot; say much more about dedicated artist than one how chop his hands and stick paint brushes in their place.</b><br /> <br /> And, by the test result in mine profile signature, I'm a first one to make Wizened character here - at least in 1ED sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-02-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T14:18:48-07:00","id":576771,"title":"","content":"Also, &quot;incorporating the tools of your trade&quot; (usually) works when your trade relies heavily on tools; but what about the Wizened who specializes in a performance art (like a singer) or a social art (like a trader)? When your craft doesn't rely on tools, what tools do you integrate? For that reason alone, I'm inclined to Wizened who aren't cyborgs. <br /> <br /> And Wyrdhamster has a point concerning dwarves, cobbler elves, and the like. I know that 2e is trying to break the bond that 1e established between Seemings and Kiths; but the fact remains that the iconic Wizened Smith is the dwarf of the Nibelung Cycle. The Kiths that were originally under the Wizened Seeming ought to resemble their 1e appearances when paired with the Wizened Seeming, at least by default. <br /> <br /> It's why I prefer the notion of &quot;you've turned your body into a finely honed instrument for performing your craft by rejecting everything that doesn't somehow serve that purpose&quot; (which <i>can</i> be interpreted as the tools of the trade cyborg if you wish, but can be interpreted in other ways) to the existing \u201cyou've replaced parts of your body with the tools of your trade\u201d notion. <br /> <br /> As well: in both cases, there's a notion that you've somehow crippled yourself in the pursuit of your art, whether you went the \u201cEdward Scissorhands\u201d route or merely reduced your size. It seems to be fundamental to the Seeming (after all, \u201cWizened\u201d isn't a reference to wisdom; it's a reference to being &quot;shriveled up&quot;). So maybe that should be the non-Breaking Point part of the Curse: you take a Persistent Condition that can never be resolved so long as you're Wizened and that represents some sort of physical handicap. Diminutive size is a common one, but hardly the only choice: the blind Oracle is another classic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T14:44:05-07:00","id":576792,"title":"","content":"I'm with Dataweaver and Arcane, both are good options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:24:15-07:00","id":576807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576647#post576647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still feels more like a Batman villian than someone who's really into their craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, every splat is a Batman villain.<br /> <br /> This has more to do with Batman than the nWoD I think. And because most of his rogues are almost as distinctive than he is (seriously, I could describe even one of the more obscure and even a couple of the more casual fans will recognize them. For example: Avian-themed soldier working for the elite).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-02-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:41:12-07:00","id":576819,"title":"","content":"Allow yourself to read expansively. All things and more possible within the Seemings.<br /> <br /> Or at least, I've yet to feel limited by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T19:29:56-07:00","id":576984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576819#post576819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow yourself to read expansively. All things and more possible within the Seemings.<br /> <br /> Or at least, I've yet to feel limited by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, this is your go-to response whenever someone doesn't feel like something written in the books is clear or sounds limited.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just read it harder! You're not reading it deeply enough&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a little, condescending, perhaps? :|","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T20:04:33-07:00","id":577016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576984#post576984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little, condescending, perhaps? :|</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone for whom criticism and the observation thereof was a formative part of their internet career and who's gotten the &quot;you're being condescending&quot; line often enough to be able to cite it: No, it's not, and this is a uselessly vague criticism to make of anybody, because there is no way to make the otherwise-inoffensive statement of &quot;you appear to be reading more specificity into the text than is actually necessary&quot; without tripping the incredibly widely-cast snare of &quot;you're telling someone that they have exhibited a shortcoming in any sense at all&quot; that you're presenting as the mark of condescension. It's unhelpful and I don't think anyone cares for it. Please refrain.<br /> <br /> Back on the actual subject of Wizened: Have people forgotten the existence of Nick Chopper as an archetype of the metaphor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T20:48:27-07:00","id":577057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576984#post576984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to admit, this is your go-to response whenever someone doesn't feel like something written in the books is clear or sounds limited.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just read it harder! You're not reading it deeply enough&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a little, condescending, perhaps? :|</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that I answered the &quot;Are they the art or the tools of the art?&quot; with &quot;Both&quot;, and that such an answer not only fits with the ideas present in that conversation but also the text.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's condescending or not, because I am not other people. I try hard not to do that, and while I know I don't always succeed, I like to think I do a good job. But in the end, if people read it as such, there's little I can do.<br /> <br /> It <i>is</i>, however, normally very applicable, particularly given the balances that White Wolf/Onyx Path have always walked with the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Either way, the matter of my condescension does not contribute to the dialogue on the Wizened.* Encouraging more readings and contemplation of the text might.<br /> <br /> *But in all seriousness, if you want to know my thoughts and feelings on the matter, PM me. I will say I have very mixed feelings about the fanbase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-03-2015, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T21:59:44-07:00","id":577074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577016#post577016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on the actual subject of Wizened: Have people forgotten the existence of Nick Chopper as an archetype of the metaphor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. He's definitely a Metalflesh; but the bit about being chopped up and replaced piecemeal with metal parts is hardly unique to the Wizened. And Nick's missing a crucial element to being a Wizened: his skill as a woodman isn't really all that important to who he is. No; what defines him is his love \u2014 originally for Nimmie Ammie, but later generalized to a broad compassion. Oddly enough, I'd probably peg him as a Fairest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:20:11-07:00","id":577083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577074#post577074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No; what defines him is his love \u2014 originally for Nimmie Ammie, but later generalized to a broad compassion. Oddly enough, I'd probably peg him as a Fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I meant &quot;as an example of the character-type,&quot; I would not have said &quot;as an archetype of the metaphor&quot; when referring to a fairy-tale character who had parts of himself replaced so that he could continue to do the task that made up half his name in both incarnations instead of naming a more abstractly relevant comparison like David's bit about all the Seemings being represented in the gang from Leverage.<br /> <br /> The Wizened's definition of themselves by their capability to perform a task and the consequent symbolic representation of function over form in their mien appeals to the archetype of the monomaniacal savant. That Nick Chopper's &quot;replace my entire body with metal and continue chopping wood&quot; metamorphosis into the Tin Woodsman a la the Ship of Theseus is a striking visual the Wizened might logically draw on does not by nature imply any statement that Nick Chopper is an example of a Wizened character.<br /> <br /> It's still a damn sight more aesthetically and thematically relevant than calling the Seeming &quot;Robocop wannabes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:38:51-07:00","id":577092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576984#post576984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to admit, this is your go-to response whenever someone doesn't feel like something written in the books is clear or sounds limited.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just read it harder! You're not reading it deeply enough&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a little, condescending, perhaps? :|</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what's happening is that a lot of people are performing a fairly strict reading of the text and using that to justify the narrowness of the splat. They're not using the text as material for inspiration for characters; they're using it as legal wording where you at best loophole and at worst restrict possibility. This is in a gameline where there are two to three less-than-official Seemings on the side, as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure why this is happening. I tend to approach this stuff from an exegetical point of view, which makes it hard to relate to how other people come at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T23:09:54-07:00","id":577101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577083#post577083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a damn sight more aesthetically and thematically relevant than calling the Seeming &quot;Robocop wannabes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough; and you'll never catch me using that phrase. \u201cCyborgs\u201d, sure; because someone who is part man and part machine <i>is</i> a cyborg. And it's not an invalid concept; if I remember the movie correctly, Edward Scissorhands would definitely qualify as a Wizened whose hands got replaced by scissor-blades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T23:41:20-07:00","id":577108,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a disconnect between the seeming description and the kith/wizened combinations.<br /> <br /> With the seeming description, it really seems to stress the character being a virtuoso at something, while in the kith descriptions it's always about the wizened being better the kith thanks to their transformation.<br /> <br /> So while it certainly would make sense for a keeper to change someone based on the aptitudes they already have, if you don't want to work it that way in your backstory, then the wizened seeming would be about a character who used their kith blessing to escape.<br /> <br /> A brollachan that just sneaked out of arcadia, a gravewright who convinced a ghost to help her escape, a levinquick who just ran, a maker who went all Tony Stark on his keeper, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T00:19:12-07:00","id":577122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577092#post577092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure why this is happening. I tend to approach this stuff from an exegetical point of view, which makes it hard to relate to how other people come at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not obvious?<br /> <br /> Different people are different. Different cultures, different backgrounds, different nationalities, maybe even nerological conditions.<br /> <br /> Some people are more literal minded than others. There's really nothing more to it than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T00:22:06-07:00","id":577125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576771#post576771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Wyrdhamster has a point concerning dwarves, cobbler elves, and the like. I know that 2e is trying to break the bond that 1e established between Seemings and Kiths; but the fact remains that the iconic Wizened Smith is the dwarf of the Nibelung Cycle. The Kiths that were originally under the Wizened Seeming ought to resemble their 1e appearances when paired with the Wizened Seeming, at least by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for mentioning this one. I think that Fairy Tale archetypes should be base of <b>all</b> Seemings, either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576771#post576771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well: in both cases, there's a notion that you've somehow crippled yourself in the pursuit of your art, whether you went the \u201cEdward Scissorhands\u201d route or merely reduced your size. It seems to be fundamental to the Seeming (after all, \u201cWizened\u201d isn't a reference to wisdom; it's a reference to being &quot;shriveled up&quot;). So maybe that should be the non-Breaking Point part of the Curse: you take a Persistent Condition that can never be resolved so long as you're Wizened and that represents some sort of physical handicap. Diminutive size is a common one, but hardly the only choice: the blind Oracle is another classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this totally - Persistent Condition pointing to physical problems for the Wizened should be main part of 2ED Curse - either way, you sacrificed some part of your body or life to the Art. Even if you have new axes in places of hands, you still have problem with operating them as they would be your normal hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577101#post577101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough; and you'll never catch me using that phrase. \u201cCyborgs\u201d, sure; because someone who is part man and part machine <i>is</i> a cyborg. And it's not an invalid concept; if I remember the movie correctly, Edward Scissorhands would definitely qualify as a Wizened whose hands got replaced by scissor-blades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Edward character in movie, but still I think those kind of characters need to be minority in Seeming - not impossible, just rare. Like maybe 20-30% of whole Wizened Seeming, not half of it like they are now n Kiths preview. Others should be more proper Fairy Tale craftsman spend years on working or dedicated oracles who lose the eyes to have better Sight of Future. Wizened should be about <i><b>Sacrifice for Art</b></i>, in various forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-03-2015, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T02:53:08-07:00","id":577185,"title":"","content":"On a darkest note, what may be considered &quot;art&quot; could have very ample and twisted interpretations. Ej: Doctor Rick Trager from Ourlast could be an example of a deranged Wizened Chirugeon in love with his &quot;work&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-03-2015, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T11:42:16-07:00","id":577556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=577122#post577122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not obvious?<br /> <br /> Different people are different. Different cultures, different backgrounds, different nationalities, maybe even nerological conditions.<br /> <br /> Some people are more literal minded than others. There's really nothing more to it than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this help me relate to other perspectives, exactly? I know you're different from me. I can tell, because we've got different screennames and everything. That doesn't actually help me understand where you're coming from or why you're seeing what you're seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T19:51:35-07:00","id":578067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576807#post576807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, every splat is a Batman villain.<br /> <br /> This has more to do with Batman than the nWoD I think. And because most of his rogues are almost as distinctive than he is (seriously, I could describe even one of the more obscure and even a couple of the more casual fans will recognize them. For example: Avian-themed soldier working for the elite).</div> </div> </div> </div>....I might need to pull out the Court Creation rules to create one that was based on being Batman's Rogue's Gallery, with Batman and co as Huntsmen. Could be a fun court for San Diego or Milwaukee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T20:12:32-07:00","id":578079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=576771#post576771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;incorporating the tools of your trade&quot; (usually) works when your trade relies heavily on tools; but what about the Wizened who specializes in a performance art (like a singer) or a social art (like a trader)? When your craft doesn't rely on tools, what tools do you integrate? For that reason alone, I'm inclined to Wizened who aren't cyborgs.<br /> <br /> And Wyrdhamster has a point concerning dwarves, cobbler elves, and the like. I know that 2e is trying to break the bond that 1e established between Seemings and Kiths; but the fact remains that the iconic Wizened Smith is the dwarf of the Nibelung Cycle. The Kiths that were originally under the Wizened Seeming ought to resemble their 1e appearances when paired with the Wizened Seeming, at least by default.<br /> <br /> It's why I prefer the notion of &quot;you've turned your body into a finely honed instrument for performing your craft by rejecting everything that doesn't somehow serve that purpose&quot; (which <i>can</i> be interpreted as the tools of the trade cyborg if you wish, but can be interpreted in other ways) to the existing \u201cyou've replaced parts of your body with the tools of your trade\u201d notion.<br /> <br /> As well: in both cases, there's a notion that you've somehow crippled yourself in the pursuit of your art, whether you went the \u201cEdward Scissorhands\u201d route or merely reduced your size. It seems to be fundamental to the Seeming (after all, \u201cWizened\u201d isn't a reference to wisdom; it's a reference to being &quot;shriveled up&quot;). So maybe that should be the non-Breaking Point part of the Curse: you take a Persistent Condition that can never be resolved so long as you're Wizened and that represents some sort of physical handicap. Diminutive size is a common one, but hardly the only choice: the blind Oracle is another classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about this a bit and trying to figure out how I'd do, say, an elvish toymaker who's Durance was working in Santa's Sweatshop. In 1e, I'd make a Wizened and in 2e I'd... create a Maker or Artisan. That realization was when I really understood the change they're doing between 1e and 2e. In 1e, that crafter elf is a Wizened. In 2e, that crafter Elf could be any Seeming, depending on how they escaped.<br /> <br /> I knew this, but I'm not sure I quite emotionally grasped it before.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what that means is that possibly some people are still hung up in that 1e way of thinking. Alternately, it's possible that a character who was a Wizened in 1e might not be in 2e. Like, if your crafter elf watched the yeti guardsmen, figured out their routes, and used some stolen tools to cut their shackles, murder the guards, and cut their way to freedom, then they're probably actually an Ogre under 2e rulers. Or, if you got a bunch of the other elves together and went on strike, then you're a Fairest.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking about it a bit more, the descriptions on some of these could use a bit more amplification on how the escape worked, maybe? I mean, lines like &quot;With this new body, the choice to devote herself to the thing that brings safety, comfort, and praise, she abandons the human parts that failed her, and with that choice, she escapes.&quot; and &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fairest has a change of heart, and changes the hearts and minds of those around him, and in that moment, he escapes.&quot; are nicely pithy, but ...well, I just hope the book will have some nice examples in it.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:56:10-07:00","id":578379,"title":"","content":"When I read the description of the Wizened Artist when the kiths were posted, I did <a href=\"http://fav.me/d8ryhdr\" target=\"_blank\">this digital painting</a>. I interpereted the bits about its form being altered to perform its art as a magical warping and twisting of its natural body, rather than prosthesis or implants. Now that I've read the new version of the Wizened Seeming, I feel like this character in the painting would more likely be a darkling or possibly have no seeming. In fact, I find that a lot of the Wizened characters from my old games now seem more suited to Darkling. In a few cases they would have probably been Ogres or Elementals. On the other hand, several Elemental characters (and one Fairest PC) from my old games would probably be Wizened in 2e. It's definitely a big shakeup.<br /> <br /> Der Ring des Nibelungen was mentioned earlier, and it got me thinking that, really, the Dwarfs from Wagner's operas would be much more likely to be Darklings in 2e. They're villainous bastards who are prone to play dirty and who manipulate the heroes like chumps. And Alberich gains his magical powers after he renounces love; that sounds pretty Darkling-y to me. More broadly, mythological dwarfs could be just about any seeming. Some are blood thirsty and violent (Ogres). Some are creepy lust-fueled perverts (Beasts). Some are associated with death (Darklings). And they are sometimes thought to be a kind of nature spirit (Elemental). The point is, the core ideas that make a Dwarf a Dwarf are tied much more to Kith and cultural background than to Seeming. A Dwarf would essentially be a particular cultural variant of the Smith (or maybe Maker) Kith, but they could be any Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:10:48-07:00","id":578389,"title":"","content":"I like that painting! I think the look could still fit a wizened. You could say his hair is now bristled like the brush he uses, and that his body is warped like wood. He has been molded into a paint brush to reflect the tool of his art.<br /> <br /> I think the look your Changeling has will be less the result of Seeming and more kith and player decision.The Devs have said it won't be obvious for other Changelings to tell what the seeming is, so there should be plenty of scope for players to decide how they look. I am partial to the idea that seeming has a subtle effect on look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T03:37:33-07:00","id":579688,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the whole thread, so apologies if this has already been discussed, but is it me or are some Wizened example kiths backward? The kith is what your keeper did to you, the Seeming is what you did to yourself, right? But in the kith list, some Wizened examples look more like self-modification.<br /> <br /> Say you're... a bodyguard. You're very motivated about bodyguarding. You get stolen away and your keeper makes you a part of his retinue of guards and turns you into a Draconic. Why do you look like a man in a dragon suit? You're not the one who turned yourself into a dragon, your keeper is. Shouldn't you look like a normal dragon-man with, I don't know, plates of armor crudely welded over the many scars you've accumulated doing your endless, thankless job? (Or some other appropriate additions for other occupations.)<br /> <br /> Unrelated, but now I want to make a character who had a friendly, gregarious personality, the sort of person you might describe as <i>warm</i>. They get abducted and turned into their keeper's forge fire, then escape by using the tools at hand to bind themselves back into human form (and thus be able to interact with others). Result: a humanoid fire with bands of steel around their limbs and a fixed, smiling metal mask for a face. Bam: Wizened ifrit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 07-05-2015, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T03:57:10-07:00","id":579690,"title":"","content":"Question: some of the old kiths, like Chatelaine or Drudge... How would they fit with the new Wizeneds and their artistic passion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T04:08:29-07:00","id":579693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=579690#post579690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: some of the old kiths, like Chatelaine or Drudge... How would they fit with the new Wizeneds and their artistic passion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your keeper didn't necessarily make you perform your art/craft/whatever. You could be a Drudge (or any other kith) and escape thanks to your deep passion for rock climbing.<br /> <br /> Sure, if being a painter is an important part of your character, it's tempting to pick the Artist kith so you can get a bonus to your painting, but you don't <i>have</i> to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:36:52-07:00","id":579751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=579690#post579690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: some of the old kiths, like Chatelaine or Drudge... How would they fit with the new Wizeneds and their artistic passion?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it has to be an <i>art</i>, per say. Maybe the Drudge escaped using her skill at taming animals, or maybe the Chatelaine used his impeccable knowledge of social protocol to trick his Keeper to let him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:18:34-07:00","id":581895,"title":"","content":"I don't recall who exactly said it, but I agree with the person earlier who said that it would feel a little more... well, &quot;wizened&quot; if the change was just &quot;forged a perfect body for themselves by losing anything that held them back from their work,&quot; with the transhuman implantation bits optional but present. As it is, the main thematic emphasis of the Seeming, visually, is less &quot;wizened&quot; than it is &quot;reconstructed,&quot; since the descriptions all mention what's been replaced, rather than what's been lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:42:30-07:00","id":582443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=579688#post579688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the whole thread, so apologies if this has already been discussed, but is it me or are some Wizened example kiths backward? The kith is what your keeper did to you, the Seeming is what you did to yourself, right? But in the kith list, some Wizened examples look more like self-modification.<br /> <br /> Say you're... a bodyguard. You're very motivated about bodyguarding. You get stolen away and your keeper makes you a part of his retinue of guards and turns you into a Draconic. Why do you look like a man in a dragon suit? You're not the one who turned yourself into a dragon, your keeper is. Shouldn't you look like a normal dragon-man with, I don't know, plates of armor crudely welded over the many scars you've accumulated doing your endless, thankless job? (Or some other appropriate additions for other occupations.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, um, no comment from anyone? It seemed like a legitimate concern to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:58:53-07:00","id":582451,"title":"","content":"If no one else has commented by later tonight, I will give my own thoughts to explain as best I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T10:22:18-07:00","id":582476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=582443#post582443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, um, no comment from anyone? It seemed like a legitimate concern to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just offhand\u2026<br /> <br /> You're rebuilding yourself &quot;from the ground up&quot; with Arcadian symbolism and the parts of yourself that you have to work with, bearing in mind that both of those include the kith that only took because it resonated with you in the first place; a Wizened Draconic bodyguard remakes themselves as a dragon-man because &quot;dragon-parts&quot; is the class of Faerie symbolism closest to hand (and formerly heart) that has sympathy with protection and intimidation.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that the kith-appearance that your seeming modifies is the baseline form of whatever transformation your Keeper inflicted upon you, which may or may not have been more involved than &quot;humanoid dragon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-07-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T10:41:20-07:00","id":582491,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I see that Satchel has said most of what I have with many fewer words and more coherently. I applaud this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=582443#post582443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, um, no comment from anyone? It seemed like a legitimate concern to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's an illegitimate concern. It's more that I feel the Kith examples are going more for clarity in the sorts of emergent aesthetics. Especially with very tight wordcount, I got a sense the goal was to give good &quot;at a glance&quot; examples, for which it's best to go about that with something simple and straightforward, rather than confuse the imagery.<br /> <br /> Like, take one of the Gentry described in the Kith's opening section, which mentioned a fondness for &quot;elegant mechanical men and attractive humanoid animals.&quot; It may just be my own reading, but I don't anticipate that the Kith for every Changeling in that realm will necessarily reflect the aesthetic. I imagine Antiquarians, Artists, Smiths, and others would still emerge there, just with mechanical or bestial traits that don't necessarily provide an impact. When a Changeling reforges herself with a Seeming, mechanically incidental traits of that sort could remain in the Mien. However, it's easy to see how such traits could muddy up what a Seeming example is actually doing, given the focused wordcount. The Wizened Artist example may happen to have, say, a jackal's head, but that wouldn't really be a relevant detail for what it's trying to get across.<br /> <br /> In the pursuit of that goal, for the Wizened, there may be a simplifying assumption that the particular Wizened's art lines up with the Kith. This does create a bit of oddness in the dragon example, for instance; I'm also a little unclear about what art that Wizened is actually enhancing, there. I'd personally feel that your description makes more sense to me, though I also admit that &quot;dragon suit&quot; wasn't the impression that the original gave me.<br /> <br /> Though there's also the possibility that, say, this is just the end result we're seeing after leaving Arcadia, the &quot;simplification&quot; of a form too complex to exist in the real world. Perhaps the Draconic, in becoming a Wizened, became even more a dragon than he already was, accomplished by stitching the bodies of dead dragons to oneself. It created a colossal, many winged and many mawed monstrosity, adding their power to one's own. In leaving Arcadia, the draconic power the Changeling attached to himself was deemed most central to its personal narrative, to the point that the draconic traits &quot;underneath&quot; just aren't expressed in the Mien.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, I've heard other ideas that causality and time are a little wonky in Arcadia. They argue that taking back agency in adopting a Seeming retroactively adjusts and reframes a Changeling's entire story. Sure, in the &quot;original&quot; tale the Keeper spun, the guy was magicked into an honest-to-goodness dragon. But it's in the nature of stories that they change with the teller, albeit keeping some of the core idea -- where &quot;core idea&quot; can also vary by the teller. In reclaiming her agency, the story stopped being about how the Keeper made her a dragon and is &quot;now&quot; the story of how she cast out the weak, human parts of herself, and made herself a dragon, and so it was always so.<br /> <br /> Dunno how much I'd personally go for that last one -- probably depends on my mood, the character, etc. -- but it's a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T10:53:18-07:00","id":582500,"title":"","content":"As a thought, just about everything we do these days usually carries an element of artistry today, and I'll argue that anything can be turned into artistry. Art is essentially a vehicle for communication, and we can communicate in a lot of different ways and on a lot of different things.<br /> <br /> So, treading on an old thread of mine, try looking at it broadly. What is the artistry of being a dragon, the patterns and forms associated with the icon that can be perfected and dwelled in as a practice? THere is an art to styles of living, an art in striding and glancing, and so there is an art of being a dragon. Some Wizened might focus on what the Dragon is used to say, some might simply focus on creating an icon to be filled, but they would look at it as an actor might look at their job of being a security guard or a cook.<br /> <br /> I might say more later, but I wanted to drop this out in unison with the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:47:11-07:00","id":582570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=582491#post582491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially with very tight wordcount, I got a sense the goal was to give good &quot;at a glance&quot; examples, for which it's best to go about that with something simple and straightforward, rather than confuse the imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, exactly my concern. Are we expecting new players to ponder the artistry of being a dragon just so they can understand the example kiths, which are there to help them get a grip on the concept? It's not that a Wizened whose thing is &quot;being a dragon&quot; doesn't sound interesting, it is, but it might not be the most simple and straightforward way of presenting things. I feel the Wizened write-up itself makes appropriate nods to concepts that are more &quot;out there&quot;, and the kith section should probably concentrate on the basic idea of the Wizened who does/crafts things.<br /> <br /> The Manikin should probably look like a robot that was extensively modified for a certain purpose instead of a robot that looks like it was once human. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T13:00:35-07:00","id":582665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=582570#post582570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is, in fact, exactly my concern. Are we expecting new players to ponder the artistry of being a dragon just so they can understand the example kiths, which are there to help them get a grip on the concept? It's not that a Wizened whose thing is &quot;being a dragon&quot; doesn't sound interesting, it is, but it might not be the most simple and straightforward way of presenting things. I feel the Wizened write-up itself makes appropriate nods to concepts that are more &quot;out there&quot;, and the kith section should probably concentrate on the basic idea of the Wizened who does/crafts things.<br /> <br /> The Manikin should probably look like a robot that was extensively modified for a certain purpose instead of a robot that looks like it was once human. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flexibility of character concept is a stated goal of the current system. Again, all things are possible.<br /> <br /> That said, of course some match ups are not going to be as intuitive, and there's only so much space that can be given to Kith example(although Dave's idea of pushing non-intuitive match ups as examples can go far, and I imagine some of the revisions to the Kith section will push the boundaries of that even further), but that's the beauty of the system-people can go for easy match-ups or hard match ups. People can find their own balance to them. You can have a Manikin that looks like it fills a singular purpose AND a Manikin that's a robot that looks like it was once human. Don't think you can make sense of a Wizened Draconic? Then don't worry about it. Got an idea of how to do it? Go for it.<br /> <br /> There's a balance between suggesting a direction and encouraging creative interpretation at work here, but I think that fits in with what people were doing with Seeming and Kith anyways-mixing and matching to create a unique and personal icon. The system now point more at a meaning of the creation of any given icon.<br /> <br /> I think as it is, most people can intuit the Kiths that are the easiest to slot into the idea of Wizened's artistry focus. Some of this will be helped a little bit by the plans to quickly group and present the Kiths for ease of selection.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, I can still see the issue, but I feel more optimistic about how it's received than not.<br /> <br /> But then again, I'm still pretty optimistic about the entire affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T22:20:23-07:00","id":583197,"title":"","content":"Small note to mention that when I say &quot;The Manikin should probably look like a robot that was extensively modified for a certain purpose instead of a robot that looks like it was once human&quot; I of course mean &quot;the <i>example</i> Manikin should probably look like etc.&quot; <i>Your</i> Manikin can look however you want it to look, obviously.<br /> <br /> It's just... if the point is to show a diversity of Wizened interpretations, then shouldn't there be some examples that aren't &quot;the appearance of the kith, except artificial&quot;, which kinda makes it look like the only acceptable modification a Wizened can make to itself is looking like their kith? Shouldn't you show that you can have a Smith who altered himself for something <i>other</i> than smithing, or a Metalflesh who, when she escaped, decided the best way to do whatever it is she does wasn't just &quot;being made out of metal&quot;, which is just the basic Metalflesh thing, but also involved welding on some spikes or turning her hands into shovels or whatever?<br /> <br /> If the point is to have a simple and straightforward presentation of the Wizened, then shouldn't you avoid things that require forumgoers to make a dissertation about the nature of causality in Arcadia to explain them? The other kith examples look like they started with the appearance of the kith, then were altered according to the Seeming. The Fairest examples look pretty, the Beast examples look beastly, etc. Following that logic, the Wizened examples should look like the appearance of the kith altered to fit a purpose. Instead, they look like humans that were altered according to the kith. Well, most do. There are one or two elemental kiths that look like the Wizened modifications are containing the elemental manifestations. Those still kinda have the problem that they don't really fit a purpose, which is the Wizened thing. The only ones that <i>do</i> look like they fit a purpose are the ones where the kith comes pre-wrapped with a purpose of its own, like Artist.<br /> <br /> I guess I just don't understand the point of view where the way things are presented right now is the <i>best</i> way to present things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T23:01:53-07:00","id":583216,"title":"","content":"The current way of presenting things isn't the best way to present things. We're looking at open-development documents. Things that haven't been finalized, or edited for tone to give the different pieces of text a sense of cohesion, or even organized together into one big thing where it makes more sense all put together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T01:50:20-07:00","id":584397,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to have a Wizened who deliberately reduced himself to an unobtrusive functionary, integrating himself unnoticed into the Gentry's household until he was able to use that invisibility to escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:42:39-07:00","id":584515,"title":"","content":"That, weirdly, kinda sound Elemental. Ha, an Elemental of Bureocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:45:54-07:00","id":584516,"title":"","content":"Making yourself psychically and physically smaller would sound wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:31:49-07:00","id":584619,"title":"","content":"Elementals let go the sense of themselves and escape by becoming part of their enviroment. Making yourself (meta)physically smaller or diminished may have been part of 1st ed Wizened but is not such a central theme of the 2nd edition splat. Not so explicitely at least, the theme of discarding aspects of yourself and substitute them for others can be seen as getting diminished. You are less and less the person you were by building up a new you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:53:09-07:00","id":584802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=584397#post584397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to have a Wizened who deliberately reduced himself to an unobtrusive functionary, integrating himself unnoticed into the Gentry's household until he was able to use that invisibility to escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that as a Wizened butler, though as Thorbes said, it could also work for an Elemental. Just depends whether the focus is more on sacrificing his body to become the ideal servant, or sacrificing his identity to become an embodiment of service.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:04:58-07:00","id":584815,"title":"","content":"THe difference between Elementals and Wizened is that the Elementals surrender their sense of self-importance and ego just shy of completely, while the Wizened completely entwine their sense of self-importance and ego up in their art.<br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind is that person could become a Draconic and then become a Wizened by devoting themselves to their violin regardless of their claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:14:28-07:00","id":584822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=584815#post584815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe difference between Elementals and Wizened is that the Elementals surrender their sense of self-importance and ego just shy of completely, while the Wizened completely entwine their sense of self-importance and ego up in their art.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good way of putting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T13:35:11-07:00","id":588435,"title":"","content":"One thing that seems to be getting forgotten is that Kith is determined by what a character did while in Arcadia, while Seeming is determined by how the character got out of Arcadia. For example: a college girl gets abducted, then turned in a crime-fighting robot, and finally escapes by grossly breaking department regs and being fired. Manikin Kith, Beast Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:25:10-07:00","id":588486,"title":"","content":"Getting forgotten by... who? Us forumgoers? The write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:58:17-07:00","id":588819,"title":"","content":"Probably forumites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T10:54:47-07:00","id":589359,"title":"","content":"A Wizened Draconic eh?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Of all the people in the world. Why did it pick an accountant to make a dragon? That's the one question I've never answered.<br /> <br /> Being a dragon isn't as fun as you might expect. You're obsessed with gold, but having it doesn't make you happy. You don't feel powerful when every knight slays you without trouble. I'm a smart man, I thought I'd stay aloft and out of reach, give them the ol firebreath. I'm still not sure how they killed me with a sword at fifty foot up, but they did. Every god damn time.<br /> <br /> The first time I died I thought enough was enough, I could fly so I picked a direction and set off. A knight got me. I tried a few more times but no matter what I did they knew if I was trying to escape. For a while I just gave up, I even started forgetting I used to be human, how to think like a human.<br /> <br /> In the end it was the princess that saved me. Not the first one I'd forced a king to sacrifice, dumb as bricks all of them. Never anything but weeping and swooning over the knight who was sure to rescue them. Well by this point I was so desperate for human conversation that I didn't care, and the knights always took a few days after a kidnapping, I was the end of the quest after all. So after a day I started getting through to her. It turns out that They made me into a dragon and her into an airhead. Once she broke through that she was a normal person again, and together we came up with a plan.<br /> <br /> Ok, she came up with the plan. She's the one who read fantasy, I read accounting, that's why I did most of the work. So this place, I suppose I should count my blessings, the peasents lived knee deep in dung and plague most of the time. Most of the kingdoms' treasuries were in my cave after all. But this time when the knight killed me he rescued a princess with a crash coarse in financial investment. It took a few kidnappings, but before long every knightly order had enough of my horde to run a few Charitable organisations. Note the capital C, it's important.<br /> <br /> Once the knights had gotten their head around the idea that material possessions can help people, she started getting them to think about how they could acquire more gold to help more people. That was the first crack in their oh-so-holy attitude. The princess gave the signal for me to abduct her again, and we waited. When the knight came she walked out stark naked, and our plan worked. He reacted like a human being, not a walking cliche, and a knight without his virtue can't hope to fight of a 60 foot fire breathing armoured lizard with a piece of sharp metal. After he was dead, I hope it wasn't permanent, it never was for me, I took the princess and we flew off. Not one fucking knight to be seen.<br /> <br /> We make an odd pair. A princess who looks like a wounded lion and a dragon who looks like an accountant; but everyone's odd around here. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, I definitely imagine him looking like a cross between a dragon and an old wise sage type. <a href=\"http://adjl.wikia.com/wiki/File:Character_sketch_3.png\" target=\"_blank\">Something like this</a>. Accountants don't really modify their body in the first place, and even if they could it doesn't fit the story. There are ways to make it fit, maybe his body is covered with accounting ledgers that he scratched on as self therapy to distract himself from the next knight (or that the Wyrd retroactively said he used as therapy even though he didn't). But given his story; the image is obviously hermit-sage with body modification a secondary feature at best.<br /> <br /> The Damsel in Distress kith ended up a lioness because like many Damsels she was royalty and lions are kings of beasts. Wounded animals show up a few times in faerie tales so it seemed like the perfect centre of the royalty, damsel, beast, ven diagram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-16-2015, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:08:22-07:00","id":589373,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't she also be a lioness because she broke social norms in their escape plan, waltzing out stark naked to meet the rescuing knight? Hence coloring her Kith with the image of the Beast Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:14:13-07:00","id":589386,"title":"","content":"Well yes, of course the transformation into a lioness is because she's a Beast. (BTW, I just updated it. It occurred to me that there's a cool wounded animal trope in faerie tales so now she looks injured)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:41:13-07:00","id":589555,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, I misinterpreted the relevant sentence. I read it as an explanation of why<i> her seeming is Beast</i>, rather than why she's <i>a lioness specifically.</i> Was a little confused.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T05:37:40-07:00","id":591167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=584619#post584619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elementals let go the sense of themselves and escape by becoming part of their enviroment. Making yourself (meta)physically smaller or diminished may have been part of 1st ed Wizened but is not such a central theme of the 2nd edition splat. Not so explicitely at least, the theme of discarding aspects of yourself and substitute them for others can be seen as getting diminished. You are less and less the person you were by building up a new you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't be diminished but maimed, especially with building up. I was thinking of something that would fit the dictionary definition of &quot;wizened&quot;. Elemental wouldn't fit because he isn't merging with an elemental force. Even if merging with the idea of service was possible, he's not doing, that, he trying to avoid being the target of affection or amusement until he can escape. A Changeling who did merge with &quot;service&quot; wouldn't want to escape in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T02:25:46-07:00","id":592426,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can get that. I was thinking more about bureocracy, order, rules and such rather than service. Tidy procedural order as an elemental force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:23:08-07:00","id":592898,"title":"","content":"Reading my Durance story again. Accountant -&gt; Money -&gt; Gold.<br /> <br /> So actually that question was quite easily answered; don't read too much into the charachter not understanding, it's purely the author's mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}